0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 710.5 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 708.5 Td (Value types \(`struct`, `enum`, primitive numerics\) inherit directly from) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 697.5 Td (`System.ValueType` \(which derives from `System.Object`\). Reference types \(`class`,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 686.5 Td (`interface`, `delegate`, `record class`, `string`, `object`\) inherit from `System.Object`.) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 675.5 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 673.5 Td (**Memory Location Myth Debunked**: Value types do *not* always live on the stack. Value) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 662.5 Td (types are allocated inline wherever their container is declared: local variables of value) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 651.5 Td (types inside methods reside on the Thread Stack; value type fields inside reference types) Tj ET
